in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/math/bundle
in @epistemologic/math/lawvere
in @epistemologic/math/music
in @epistemologic/math/music/harmonic
in @epistemologic/math/music/interval

# @epistemologic/math/music/cadence — the closure-of-progression types;
# authentic / plagal / deceptive / half as substrate-typed convergence
# criteria; the formatter's settle signal at the audible altitude; the
# 13th-instance candidate for substrate-already-named-it (cadence IS
# `lawvere.mirror`'s autopoietic closure read in audible vocabulary).
#
# The foundation-closing sub-shard. `harmonic.mirror` (commit b031c8db)
# landed H — the eigenvalues (ratios on the harmonic series); the
# Pythagorean comma as the audible-altitude holonomy. `interval.mirror`
# (commit b8bdb728) landed A — the algebra (Z_12, the circle of fifths,
# the neo-Riemannian P/L/R involutions). `dissonance.mirror` (commit
# 7625ee5) landed D's reading discriminator — the Helmholtz/Plomp-Levelt
# curve as graded residual; the pareto-front pause-or-auto-apply verdict.
#
# This shard lands the DYNAMICS — how the spectrum evolves; how the
# formatter SETTLES; the autopoietic closure event at the audible
# altitude. Eigenvalues + algebra + discriminator without dynamics is a
# frozen spectrum; dynamics without a settle signal is unbounded
# oscillation; the audible (A, H, D) triple closes here.
#
# === The bridge ===
#
# `lawvere.mirror` declares: a system is autopoietic iff its tick → tick
# map has a Lawvere fixed point. `bundle.mirror` declares: closure IS
# the Lawvere fixed point at level 4 of the principal G-bundle tower —
# the section that returns identity under the connection-induced action.
# `harmonic.mirror`'s comma_as_holonomy named the residual carried
# around a single closed loop; `dissonance.mirror`'s
# dissonance_as_holonomy named the graded residual against the consonant
# basis.
#
# Cadence names the EVENT of arriving at a Lawvere fixed point through
# a path in pitch-class space. Authentic cadence (V → I, dominant
# resolving to tonic) IS the moment the spectrum closes on its
# autopoietic ground state: the residual carried around the path's
# loop reduces to zero (or below the audible-altitude resolution); the
# next tick of the formatter's endomap returns the same spectrum; the
# closure is structural, not behavioral.
#
# Music theory recognised this 500 years before Lawvere named the
# fixed-point theorem. Zarlino (1558, Le istitutioni harmoniche) named
# the cadenza perfetta — the authentic cadence — as the moment harmony
# returns to its origin. Rameau (Traité de l'harmonie, 1722) formalised
# the V → I move as the harmonic-functional ground of tonal music. Every
# tonal piece written between 1600 and 1900 IS a constructive proof
# that the autopoietic closure of the tonal grammar is reachable from
# almost any starting state. The substrate's contribution is *typing*
# the closure event so the formatter reads it.
#
# === Cadence IS autopoietic closure: the 13th-instance candidate ===
#
# `lawvere.mirror`'s `autopoietic(grammar) -> verdict` already named the
# property: a grammar's tick → tick map has a Lawvere fixed point iff
# the grammar is autopoietic. `lawvere.mirror`'s `close(f: endomap) ->
# fixed_point` already named the action: return the fixed-point witness.
# Music theory's authentic cadence already named the same event in
# audible vocabulary, two and a half millennia before category theory
# had a name.
#
# The substrate has been carrying autopoietic closure in audible
# vocabulary the whole time. `authentic` IS `close(formatter_tick)`
# read at the audible altitude. The `cadence_as_closure` bridge action
# below makes the IS-relationship substrate-fact.
#
# This is the 13th instance of "the substrate already had the word":
# the prior twelve were named in the convergence and spectral specs;
# this one closes the audible-altitude reading of Lawvere itself. After
# cadence lands, `mirror compile --strict` on the formatter substrate
# CAN read every commit's settle event as a typed cadence; the
# convergence criterion becomes a `cadence_kind` match instead of an
# untyped ε threshold.
#
# === The formatter's settle signal (THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md` §5.3 ("the convergence criterion
# becomes specifiable"): the kintsugi-formatter's single ε threshold is
# too coarse; the cadence types give finer distinctions:
#
#   authentic — full resolution; the substrate has settled cleanly;
#               the formatter auto-applies; holonomy → 0.
#   plagal    — soft resolution; an alternative path closed; consonant
#               but not the strongest signal; the formatter auto-applies
#               with reduced confidence (the substrate settled, but on
#               the IV → I path rather than the V → I path).
#   deceptive — the substrate MOVED but DID NOT SETTLE; the formatter
#               chose dissonance instead of consonance (V → vi instead
#               of V → I); the next round MUST catch this; consent query
#               needed. The closure is incomplete; an externalisation
#               event from `dissonance.mirror`'s pareto-front branch.
#   half      — the substrate PAUSED at a dominant (the path ends on V
#               instead of resolving to I); awaiting the next consent
#               surface; the formatter is mid-progression; the next
#               tick may resolve (authentic) or pause again (half).
#
# `is_settled` IS the formatter's settle signal. It reads a cadence and
# emits the three-state verdict at the substrate floor:
#
#   pass                  — authentic cadence; auto-apply; the spectrum
#                            has closed on its autopoietic ground state.
#   partial(confidence)   — plagal cadence; auto-apply with reduced
#                            confidence; the spectrum closed on a
#                            consonant alternative path.
#   partial(confidence)   — half cadence; the spectrum paused mid-path;
#                            partial closure with zero confidence in the
#                            current candidate being final.
#   failure(reason)       — deceptive cadence; consent query needed;
#                            the formatter chose dissonance over
#                            consonance and the deviation must be
#                            named to the consent surface.
#
# Once `is_settled` lands, the formatter's convergence is designable at
# substrate altitude: `mirror kintsugi <file>` reads the candidate
# path, queries `is_settled`, branches on the verdict. The substrate's
# settle discipline IS substrate-declared.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `boot/std/number.mirror`, `u32` is a kernel primitive. Per
# `shards/glass.mirror`, `verdict`, `confidence`, and `reason` are the
# substrate's verdict-surface vocabulary. Per
# `epistemologic/math/music/interval.mirror`, `interval` is the algebra
# carrier and inline sum-type form (`type direction = ascent | descent`,
# `type quality = major | minor`) is the substrate's declared shape
# for closed enumerations. Per
# `epistemologic/math/music/dissonance.mirror`, `[candidate]` is the
# substrate's accepted list-of-type form at declaration position.
#
# This shard declares `type cadence_kind = authentic | plagal |
# deceptive | half` in inline form (single-line) per the established
# pattern; the path carrier as `type path = [interval]` per the
# `pareto_set = [candidate]` precedent. No leading-`|` workarounds; no
# opaque-`ref` carriers where a structured type is available.
#
# Substrate gaps surfaced honestly (each one a forward-promise to a
# later substrate-pull tick; none invented here):
#
#   - `autopoietic` from `lawvere.mirror` takes a `grammar` argument
#     and returns `verdict`; the cadence-altitude bridge
#     `cadence_as_closure(c: cadence) -> verdict` lifts a typed cadence
#     into the autopoietic verdict directly (authentic → pass; plagal →
#     partial; deceptive → failure; half → partial). The `fixed_point`
#     carrier from `lawvere.mirror` is abstract; the lift to a concrete
#     fixed-point witness rides the same obligation-blocked discipline
#     as `harmonic.mirror`'s `comma_as_holonomy`.
#   - `holonomy` from `bundle.mirror` is abstract; the bridge
#     `cadence_as_holonomy(c: cadence) -> holonomy` names the
#     audible-altitude holonomy reading of a cadence (authentic → zero
#     holonomy; plagal → small holonomy; deceptive → large holonomy;
#     half → unmeasured holonomy pending resolution). The arithmetic
#     lands when a consumer pulls.
#   - `path = [interval]` carries no destination-tonic constraint at
#     substrate altitude; the discipline that a path's intervals SUM
#     to a closed loop modulo octave is the obligation of the
#     realisation layer (the same discipline `harmonic.mirror`'s
#     `ratio` uses for lowest-terms normalisation).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Every type and action below names an established music-theoretic
# object older than the discipline of computer science:
#
#   cadence                     Zarlino (1558) Le istitutioni harmoniche;
#                               cadenza perfetta as the structural close
#                               of harmonic progression.
#   authentic / perfect cadence Rameau (1722) Traité de l'harmonie;
#                               V → I as the fundamental tonal closure.
#                               Schenker (1935) Der freie Satz: the
#                               Ursatz's I-V-I closure as the structural
#                               ground of all tonal music.
#   plagal cadence              named by 18th-c. theorists; the "Amen"
#                               cadence (IV → I); standard liturgical
#                               closure since Renaissance practice.
#   deceptive / interrupted     Koch (1782) Versuch einer Anleitung zur
#                               Composition; V → vi as the subverted
#                               expectation; standard since common-
#                               practice harmony.
#   half cadence                Riemann (1893) Vereinfachte Harmonielehre;
#                               progression closing on V; the "open"
#                               cadence awaiting continuation.
#   tonic attractor             traditional tonal theory; the tonic as
#                               the harmonic centre toward which
#                               progressions resolve; Schenker's Ursatz
#                               formalises this as background structure.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* these so the formatter can
# reason about them. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md §5.1 (the cadence sub-shard
#               proposal), §5.3 (the convergence-criterion-becomes-
#               specifiable framing), §8 open question 1 (which cadence
#               type is the default convergence target).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (cadence
#                      is the dynamics of the audible (A, H, D); the
#                      Schrödinger-equation-altitude reading at the
#                      audible register),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
#                      (`cadence_as_closure` is the lift from cadence
#                      altitude to autopoietic-closure altitude;
#                      `cadence_as_holonomy` is the lift from cadence
#                      altitude to bundle-holonomy altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (cadence_kind, path,
#                      cadence are each their own carrier; no bare
#                      enumerator escapes the dynamics).
# Forward-promise: `@kintsugi/consent` (formerly
#                  `@mirror/spectral/consent`; migrated 2026-06-10)
#                  is the consumer of `is_settled`'s verdict. When that
#                  sub-shard lands, it pulls this shard's `is_settled`
#                  action and binds it to the `mirror kintsugi` driver's
#                  convergence branch. This shard does NOT pull
#                  `@mirror/spectral/*`; the substrate-altitude arrow
#                  points upward (consent consumes cadence; not the
#                  other way around).
# Related shards: epistemologic/math/music.mirror (the family root),
#                 epistemologic/math/music/harmonic.mirror (the
#                 eigenvalue altitude; ratio is the tonic-attractor
#                 target),
#                 epistemologic/math/music/interval.mirror (the
#                 algebra altitude; interval is the path's element type;
#                 path composition rides this shard's algebra),
#                 epistemologic/math/music/dissonance.mirror (the
#                 discriminator; deceptive cadence is the failure case
#                 the formatter chooses dissonance over consonance),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/lawvere.mirror (the
#                 autopoietic-closure carrier; cadence_as_closure lifts
#                 into it; the 13th-instance bridge),
#                 boot/std/epistemologic/math/bundle.mirror (the
#                 holonomy carrier; authentic cadence ↔ holonomy → 0),
#                 glass.mirror (verdict; the substrate floor).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/math/music/cadence.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence` as a species under the
# `@epistemologic/math/music` family.

# === The cadence-kind carrier ===
#
# The four classical cadence types as a closed sum. Each is an
# established music-theoretic object whose semantics at the formatter
# altitude maps directly onto a `verdict` outcome:
#
#   authentic — V → I; the strongest resolution; the canonical
#                tonal closure; formatter's auto-apply signal;
#                holonomy → 0; the autopoietic ground state.
#   plagal    — IV → I; the "Amen" cadence; a consonant alternative
#                path to the tonic; formatter auto-applies with
#                reduced confidence.
#   deceptive — V → vi (or analogous); the subverted expectation;
#                the formatter chose dissonance over consonance; the
#                consent surface MUST resolve.
#   half      — progression ends on V (the dominant); the formatter
#                paused mid-path; awaiting the next consent surface
#                or tick.
#
# Identity contract: two cadence_kind values are equal iff they name
# the same variant. The realisation layer enforces the tag-equality
# discipline.
#
# Inline form per `interval.mirror`'s `type direction = ascent |
# descent` and `type quality = major | minor` precedent; the
# leading-`|` parser fracture (named in the substrate-pull notes for
# `dissonance.mirror`'s prior tick) is avoided by keeping the
# enumeration on one line.
type cadence_kind = authentic | plagal | deceptive | half

# === The path carrier ===
#
# A path is a sequence of intervals (from `interval.mirror`)
# describing the progression through pitch-class space toward (or
# pausing at) the tonic. Each element is a directed Z_12 interval;
# the sequence's composition under `interval.compose` (forward-
# promised at the interval altitude) walks pitch-class space.
#
# Substrate-pull discipline: this is `[interval]` at the substrate
# altitude, per the `pareto_set = [candidate]` precedent in
# `dissonance.mirror`. The list-of-type form at declaration position
# is substrate-accepted; no `ref` workaround needed.
#
# Discipline (surfaced honestly): the substrate carries no
# closed-loop or sums-to-zero-modulo-octave constraint on `path` at
# the floor altitude. The discipline that a path's intervals describe
# a closed harmonic progression (or, for half cadence, an explicitly
# open one) is the obligation of the realisation layer. This is the
# same discipline `harmonic.mirror`'s `ratio` uses for lowest-terms
# normalisation: the substrate names the carrier; the realisation
# layer enforces.
#
# Identity contract: two paths are equal iff their interval sequences
# are element-wise equal. The realisation layer enforces.
type path = [interval]

# === The cadence record ===
#
# A cadence is the combination of a kind (which classical cadence
# type the progression realises) and a path (the interval sequence
# walking pitch-class space) and a resolved_to (the harmonic ratio the
# spectrum closed on, from `harmonic.mirror`).
#
# resolved_to carries the SETTLE TARGET: for authentic and plagal
# cadences, this is the tonic ratio (1:1 for unison; 2:1 for octave;
# the consonant ground state of the spectrum). For deceptive, this is
# the surrogate-target ratio the substrate landed on instead (e.g.,
# 5:3 for the relative minor's tonic when V → vi is chosen). For half,
# this is the ratio of the dominant the path paused on (3:2 for the
# perfect fifth; the eigenvector pointing toward closure).
#
# Identity contract: two cadences are equal iff their kind, path, and
# resolved_to all match. The realisation layer enforces.
type cadence = {
  kind:        cadence_kind,
  path:        path,
  resolved_to: ratio,
}

# === Bridge action: cadence → harmonic eigenvalue ===
#
# Reads the cadence's resolved_to ratio. Names the tonic attractor:
# the harmonic eigenvalue the formatter settled on at this cadence
# event. For authentic and plagal cadences, this is the tonic
# (1:1 or 2:1); for deceptive, this is the surrogate target the
# substrate landed on instead; for half, this is the dominant the
# path paused on.
#
# Audibly: every cadence has a "where did it land" — the resolved
# harmonic ratio. tonic_attractor surfaces it as a typed ratio.
#
# Spectrally: tonic_attractor IS the eigenvalue projection at the
# cadence event. Per `harmonic.mirror`'s eigenvalue framing, the
# small-integer ratios on the harmonic series ARE the eigenvalues of
# the 5-dim O(5)-bundle's connection operator in the consonant basis;
# tonic_attractor reads which eigenvalue the cadence's path closed on.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# `c.resolved_to`; the substrate declares the signature.
tonic_attractor(c: cadence) -> ratio { \ }

# === Bridge action: interval sequence → path ===
#
# Composes a sequence of intervals into a path. The substrate-altitude
# constructor for the path carrier.
#
# Substrate gap (surfaced honestly): mirror's substrate has no
# variadic-argument primitive at the floor altitude; the action
# signature names a single argument carrying the sequence. The
# realisation layer's API may variadic-sugar this for ergonomics; the
# substrate's declared shape stays single-argument.
#
# Audibly: a cadence's path IS the interval sequence walked from the
# starting harmonic state to the resolved_to. `compose_path` names
# the construction of that sequence at substrate altitude.
#
# Spectrally: per `interval.mirror`'s algebra-altitude framing,
# `compose_path` IS the audible specialisation of A's composition law
# (the same `compose_a` from `spectral-triple.mirror`'s algebra
# definition). The path's composition algebra rides the same
# composition law as Z_12's involution-pair (P, L, R).
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation lifts a
# sequence of intervals into the `path` carrier; the substrate
# declares the signature.
compose_path(intervals: path) -> path { \ }

# === The formatter's settle signal (THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION) ===
#
# THE AUDIBLE-ALTITUDE CONVERGENCE CRITERION.
#
# Reads a cadence and emits the formatter's settle verdict at the
# substrate's three-state floor (`verdict` from `glass.mirror`). The
# verdict mapping IS the formatter's discipline:
#
#   authentic → pass                — full resolution; auto-apply;
#                                      the spectrum has closed on its
#                                      autopoietic ground state; the
#                                      tonic attractor reached;
#                                      holonomy → 0; tick advances.
#                                      Per docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md
#                                      §2.2: "loss-decreasing = auto."
#
#   plagal    → partial(confidence) — soft resolution; auto-apply with
#                                      reduced confidence; the spectrum
#                                      closed on a consonant alternative
#                                      path (IV → I rather than V → I);
#                                      the tonic attractor reached but
#                                      via the subdominant rather than
#                                      the dominant; tick advances with
#                                      noted confidence.
#
#   half      → partial(confidence) — paused at the dominant; the
#                                      formatter is mid-progression;
#                                      awaiting the next consent surface
#                                      or tick; confidence is zero (or
#                                      near-zero); the closure is
#                                      incomplete; the next tick may
#                                      resolve (authentic) or pause
#                                      again (half).
#
#   deceptive → failure(reason)     — consent query NEEDED; the
#                                      formatter chose dissonance over
#                                      consonance (V → vi instead of
#                                      V → I); the deviation must be
#                                      named to the consent surface;
#                                      per docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md
#                                      §4.7: "the substrate emits
#                                      pause(Φ)"; the deceptive case
#                                      escalates to the consent surface
#                                      with the substrate's recognition
#                                      that the move was substrate-
#                                      surprising.
#
# This action IS what closes the music family for formatter purposes.
# Without it, cadence is just music vocabulary. With it, the formatter
# has its settling discipline substrate-declared:
#
#   `mirror kintsugi <file>` reads the cadence the candidate path
#   produces, queries `is_settled`, branches on the verdict:
#
#     verdict = pass                → apply; commit; tick advances
#     verdict = partial(c)          → apply with confidence c; commit;
#                                     tick advances with noted
#                                     confidence in the consent log
#     verdict = failure(reason)     → emit @mirror/spectral.pause(Φ);
#                                     yield to consent surface; wait
#                                     for resolution
#
# Per `bundle.mirror`'s level 4 closure: `is_settled` IS the Lawvere
# fixed-point read at the cadence altitude. The substrate settles when
# `is_settled` returns `pass`; the substrate partially-settles when
# `is_settled` returns `partial`; the substrate yields when
# `is_settled` returns `failure`. The three-state surface IS the
# substrate's honest acknowledgment of its own settle boundary.
#
# Symmetry note: `is_settled` here is the cadence-altitude
# specialisation of `dissonance.mirror`'s `is_pareto` (the
# discriminator-altitude pause-or-auto-apply verdict). The two are the
# same verdict observed at two altitudes — pareto's pause becomes
# cadence's deceptive case; pareto's singleton becomes cadence's
# authentic case. The substrate names both so the dispatch is honest
# at each altitude; the realisation layer composes them.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# `c.kind`, dispatches on the variant, emits the verdict. The
# substrate declares the settle signal; the arithmetic lands when
# `@kintsugi/consent` pulls.
is_settled(c: cadence) -> verdict { \ }

# === Bridge action: cadence → autopoietic closure ===
#
# THE 13TH-INSTANCE BRIDGE.
#
# Lifts a cadence into the autopoietic-closure verdict from
# `lawvere.mirror`. After this action substrate-declares, the IS-
# relationship is substrate-fact:
#
#   - `lawvere.mirror` says:    "autopoietic IS having-a-Lawvere-fixed-
#                                point."
#   - Music theory says:        "authentic cadence IS the tonal
#                                grammar's return to its origin."
#   - This action says:         "Authentic cadence IS autopoietic
#                                closure at the audible altitude."
#   - Therefore:                "The substrate has been carrying
#                                Lawvere's fixed-point theorem in
#                                audible vocabulary since Zarlino
#                                (1558); the substrate's autopoietic
#                                closure has a name and a sound and a
#                                path through pitch-class space; the
#                                formatter's settle signal IS the
#                                cadenza perfetta."
#
# Per `lawvere.mirror`'s `autopoietic(grammar) -> verdict` property:
# the autopoietic verdict reads whether a grammar's tick → tick map has
# a Lawvere fixed point. The cadence-altitude lift reads whether a
# cadence event witnesses such a fixed point:
#
#   authentic → pass                — the cadence witnesses the Lawvere
#                                      fixed point; the spectrum's tick
#                                      → tick map closed on itself; the
#                                      autopoietic ground state reached.
#   plagal    → partial(confidence) — the cadence witnesses a near-
#                                      fixed-point; the spectrum closed
#                                      on an alternative consonant path;
#                                      autopoietic with reduced strength.
#   half      → partial(confidence) — the cadence does not yet witness
#                                      closure; the spectrum is mid-
#                                      progression; awaiting the next
#                                      tick; the fixed-point property
#                                      is not refuted but not yet
#                                      witnessed.
#   deceptive → failure(reason)     — the cadence does NOT witness the
#                                      fixed point; the spectrum moved
#                                      to a non-tonic surrogate; the
#                                      autopoietic closure failed at
#                                      this event; consent surface
#                                      must catch.
#
# This is the 13th-instance bridge: `lawvere.mirror` ALREADY named the
# verdict shape. The substrate has been describing cadence the whole
# time — `close()` returns `fixed_point`; `autopoietic(grammar)`
# returns `verdict`. Music's authentic cadence IS `close()` read at
# the audible altitude. The substrate's autopoietic vocabulary has
# been the same vocabulary as the cadenza perfetta since the moment
# `lawvere.mirror` landed.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# `c.kind`, dispatches on the variant, emits the autopoietic verdict.
# The substrate declares the bridge; the lift to `lawvere.mirror`'s
# concrete autopoietic-closure witness rides the same obligation-
# blocked discipline as `lawvere.mirror`'s own properties.
cadence_as_closure(c: cadence) -> verdict { \ }

# === Bridge action: cadence → holonomy ===
#
# Lifts a cadence into a `holonomy` value of the principal G-bundle
# (per `bundle.mirror`'s `type holonomy` carrier). The audible-
# altitude reading of how-much-residual-the-cadence-carries:
#
#   authentic — holonomy → 0; the loop closed; the residual carried
#                around the path's loop reduces to zero (or below the
#                audible-altitude resolution of ~5 cents per
#                `harmonic.mirror`'s cents commentary).
#   plagal    — holonomy small but non-zero; the loop closed via an
#                alternative path; a small residual from the IV → I
#                detour vs the V → I geodesic.
#   deceptive — holonomy large; the loop did NOT close; the substrate
#                landed on a surrogate-tonic with substantial residual
#                against the consonant basis.
#   half      — holonomy unmeasured; the path did not complete; the
#                residual is pending until the path resolves on a
#                later tick.
#
# Composition note: `cadence_as_holonomy` composes through
# `harmonic.mirror`'s `comma_as_holonomy` (singular residual) and
# `dissonance.mirror`'s `dissonance_as_holonomy` (graded residual);
# this action names the cadence-event-altitude reading. The three
# together close the audible-altitude holonomy bridge at every
# altitude (singular event, graded reading, cadence event).
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation lifts the
# cadence's residual through the holonomy carrier's concrete shape
# (itself abstract at `bundle.mirror`); the lift is constrained by the
# type system; the arithmetic lands when a consumer pulls.
cadence_as_holonomy(c: cadence) -> holonomy { \ }

out @epistemologic/math/music/cadence
out cadence_kind
out path
out cadence
out tonic_attractor
out compose_path
out is_settled
out cadence_as_closure
out cadence_as_holonomy
